8.2.m:
From food, indeed, creatures are born,
whichever dwell upon earth;
then by food alone they live,
and into it they pass at the end.
For food is the eldest of beings;
therefore it is called the universal medicine.
All food indeed they attain
who revere food as brahman.
For food is the eldest of beings;
therefore it is called the universal medicine.
From food beings are born;
born, by food they grow.
It is eaten and it eats beings;
therefore it is called food.
Distinct from this [Self] consisting of the essence of food, there is another, inner Self consisting of vital breath. By that, this is filled. That one is indeed shaped like a man. In accordance with its human shape,
this one is shaped like a man. Its head is out-breath alone; the diffused breath is the right wing; the down-breath is the left wing; space is the trunk; earth is the tail, the support. On that also there is this verse:

8.3.m:
Along with the vital breath, the gods breathe,
and humans and whatever beasts [there are];
for the vital breath is the lifespan of beings;
therefore it is called the universal lifespan.
They attain a full lifespan,
who revere the vital breath as brahman.
For the vital breath is the lifespan of beings;
therefore it is called the universal lifespan.
This is indeed the bodily Self of that former one. Distinct from this [Self] consisting of vital breath,
there is another, inner Self consisting of mind. By that, this is filled. That one is indeed shaped like a man. In accordance with its human shape, this one is shaped like a man. Its head is the Yajus alone; the Ṛg is the right wing; the Sāman is the left wing; the injunction is the trunk; the Atharvāṅgirases are the tail, the support. On that also there is this verse:
